{
  "dom_id": "step-q1356",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let  $\\overset{\\to }{u}=⟨6,2,7⟩$ and $\\overset{\\to }{v}=⟨-3,-1,3⟩.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{u}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{v}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{u}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{v} & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-1)+(7)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-18-2+21 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
